1
00:00:00,316 --> 00:00:01,776
(Raj:)Feel better now?

2
00:00:01,942 --> 00:00:05,492
It's indigenous to Brazil, as is the cocoa
bean from which we get chocolate.

3
00:00:05,654 --> 00:00:08,074
(Sheldon:)You promised
you wouldn't do that anymore.

4
00:00:09,492 --> 00:00:12,582
- Hey, Hofstadter.
- Hey, Kripke.

5
00:00:12,745 --> 00:00:14,875
Heard about your anti-proton
decay experiment.

6
00:00:15,039 --> 00:00:18,209
Twenty thousand data runs
and no statistically significant results.

7
00:00:18,375 --> 00:00:20,545
Very impressive.

8
00:00:22,213 --> 00:00:23,713
(Howard:)What a jerk.

9
00:00:23,881 --> 00:00:27,171
(Raj:)Don't feel bad, Leonard.
Negative results are still results.

10
00:00:27,343 --> 00:00:30,223
- Even 20,000 of them.
- All right.

11
00:00:31,514 --> 00:00:33,434
(Leonard:)Please don't cheer me up anymore.

12
00:00:33,599 --> 00:00:35,889
Come on, don't let him get to you.
It's Kripke.

13
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:38,560
(Raj:)Yeah, he's a ginormous knob.

14
00:00:38,729 --> 00:00:42,859
(Howard:)That's why he eats by himself
instead of sitting here at the cool table.

15
00:00:43,359 --> 00:00:45,439
For shizzle.

16
00:00:48,614 --> 00:00:52,614
(Sheldon:)Hey, it's true, Kripke lacks the basic
social skills that we take for granted.

17
00:00:53,953 --> 00:00:56,203
But he controls
the new Open Science Grid computer...

